    },
    "You're still reaching for arrows %lld%% of the time" : {

    },
    "You're using `i` to enter insert before the cursor. `a` enters insert just after — saves a `→` press whenever you're inserting at the end of a word." : {

    },
    "You're using operators like `d`, `c`, `y`. The next step is text objects — `daw` deletes a whole word including its space, `ci\"` changes everything inside the next quote pair. Ten new combinations, one mental model." : {

    },
    "You've internalised hjkl. The next motion to add is `w` (jump to next word) and `b` (jump back). They're how vim users skip across a line without holding `l`." : {

